  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="HHEBA1CD44839C108D1DAFD6DE3427BE45" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="HH22FBAEA0509E80B804A4341B1670898A" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #242424; font-family: 'Aptos Narrow', Calibri, 'sans-serif', 'Mongolian Baiti', 'Microsoft Yi Baiti', 'Javanese Text', 'Yu Gothic'; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;"&gt;9. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: #242424; font-family: 'Aptos Narrow', Calibri, 'sans-serif', 'Mongolian Baiti', 'Microsoft Yi Baiti', 'Javanese Text', 'Yu Gothic'; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;"&gt;On July 18, 2018, in Docket No. PL17-1-001, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("Commission") dismissed the requests for rehearing and clarification of its revised policy statement on treatment of income taxes and provided guidance regarding the treatment of accumulated deferred income taxes ("ADIT") in light of its revised policy. Inquiry Regarding the Commissions Policy for Recovery of Income Tax Costs, Order on Rehearing of Revised Policy Statement, 164 FERC 61,030 (Jul 18, 2018). Pursuant to the guidance provided by the Commission in its July 18 Order, Texas Eastern Transmission, LP, an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of (a tax pass-through entity owned in part by) Spectra Energy Partners, LP , a master limited partnership, intends to remove any balances recorded in Accounts 190, 281, 282, and 283 of the Commission's Uniform System of Accounts, as well as excess ADIT that has been transferred to Account 254 and deficient ADIT that has been transferred to Account 182.3. Texas Eastern has requested approval in Docket No. AC18-220 from the Chief Accountant of the Commission to implement the accounting entries necessary for removing these balances. The request is currently pending. Upon receipt of the Chief Accountant's approval, Texas Eastern will reflect the removal of these balances in the annual and quarterly financing reporting required by Part 260 of the Commission's regulations. On November 27, 2023, SEP, a subsidiary of Enbridge Inc., filed with the Commission in Docket No. AC18-220-000 a request on behalf of certain of SEP's pipeline and affiliates, including Texas Eastern, for a Motion for Action on its September 10, 2018, request for approval of accounting entries in this proceeding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="HH582A4E700260C05D782FA2D6F218758A" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock id="HHE60759687E403C6B3DE58B8464A791E0" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #242424; font-family: 'Aptos Narrow', Calibri, 'sans-serif', 'Mongolian Baiti', 'Microsoft Yi Baiti', 'Javanese Text', 'Yu Gothic'; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;"&gt;11. On June 3, 2024, Texas Eastern filed its petition for approval of the Stipulation and Agreement related to the May 3, 2024, prepackaged 2024 settlement, and on July 31, 2024, Texas Eastern received approval from the FERC of its uncontested rate settlement; Pursuant to the July 2024 Order and the 2024 Settlement, Texas Eastern is required to file two actual tariff records reflecting rate effective dates of October 1, 2024, and January 1, 2026. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #242424; font-family: 'Aptos Narrow', Calibri, 'sans-serif', 'Mongolian Baiti', 'Microsoft Yi Baiti', 'Javanese Text', 'Yu Gothic'; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;"&gt;Pursuant to the July 2024 Order and terms of the 2024 Settlement, on September 3, 2024 and November 7, 2025, Texas Eastern filed actual tariff records reflecting rate effective dates of October 1, 2024 and January 1, 2026, respectively. Texas Eastern will continue to operate under those rates effective January 1, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="HHC9E9219375AC2F82A8CDFAF00D88FECC" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="ewa-rteLine"&gt;12. Uses the officers of its General Partner, Spectra Energy Transmission Services, LLC:&lt;/div&gt;
